# Waypoint architecture

Sources of truth: `docs/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md` (architecture), `docs/SRS.md` (functional requirements).
If they are ambiguous or conflict, ask. Never invent business rules.

## Stack and layout
- TypeScript strict everywhere (`strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`). No `any`.
- pnpm workspace monorepo. PostgreSQL 16.
- `apps/web`: React + Vite PWA. `apps/api`: Fastify.
- `packages/shared`: Zod schemas, status enums, DTOs, error codes. Use these; never redefine statuses or payloads locally.
- `packages/planning`: pure deterministic engine. May import `packages/shared` only.
  Never touches the database, HTTP, environment variables, `Date.now()` / `new Date()` without arguments, or browser APIs. The caller passes the current time.
- `packages/database`: Drizzle schema, migrations, seed.
- Do not add libraries without explaining why. Do not replace chosen technologies without permission.

## API
- HTTP route -> service -> repository. Routes never query Drizzle directly.
- Role authorization and resource scoping are enforced server-side (`requireRole`, `scope(user)`). Frontend role checks are never security.
- Out-of-scope records return 404, not 403.

## Planning
- Every hard constraint (SYSTEM_DESIGN §7.2) is authoritative.
- Recommendation and allocation logic ranks feasible options only and never bypasses the validator.

## Client state
- Server data: TanStack Query. Zustand: UI state only. Driver offline data: Dexie.
- Driver actions are local-first, synced through an idempotent outbox. Every client event has a unique `client_event_id`.
- Never silently resolve sync conflicts.

## Time
- All operational times are interpreted in `Asia/Colombo`.

## State machines
- Use SYSTEM_DESIGN §5.3 for order, trip, stop, loading and sync states (decided over SRS §16.1 / §43).

## Code
- Small modules, reusable components. No fake APIs or mock data in production feature code.
- Keep the app runnable after every milestone. Don't rewrite working unrelated modules.
